# Authentication

Auth strategy: `{{AUTH_STRATEGY}}`. Target URLs: `{{TARGET_URLS_JSON}}`. Runtime version: `{{AUTH_RUNTIME_VERSION}}`.

## Providers

This skill delegates all cookie / SSO handling to two independently-published
tools rather than reimplementing them in-tree:

| Strategy | Order tried |
|---|---|
| `jd-internal` | `erp-sso-login` → `browser-auth-cookie` |
| `browser-cookie` | `browser-auth-cookie` only |
| `none` | *no cookie header attached* |

Configure them once per machine, not per skill.

### `browser-auth-cookie` (universal fallback)

```bash
pip install browser-auth-cookie
```

Reads cookies from any currently-signed-in browser (Edge, Chrome, Firefox,
Safari, Chromium, Brave, Opera, Vivaldi). Order can be customised with
`BROWSER_AUTH_BROWSERS=edge,chrome,firefox`.

### `erp-sso-login` (京东内网优先)

Only needed for JD internal targets (`*.jd.com`). Set:

```bash
export ERP_SSO_LOGIN_HOME=/path/to/erp-sso-login   # skill directory
```

The runtime shells out to `${ERP_SSO_LOGIN_HOME}/assets/scripts/run.sh --url <target> --cookie-header`.
京ME 桌面客户端必须已登录。

## Overrides

- `BROWSER_FORGE_COOKIE_HEADER` — bypass discovery, use the given `Cookie:`
  header verbatim (for CI / one-off scripts).
- Command-level `--refresh-auth` — discard the in-process cache and force a
  fresh SSO / browser read on the next request.

## Never do this

- Never write a real `Cookie:` value into `manifest.json` or any repo file.
- Never log unredacted cookie values (the runtime's `RedactingFilter` strips
  them; keep it enabled).

## Diagnostics

```bash
scripts/{{ENTRYPOINT_NAME}} doctor      # provider availability
scripts/{{ENTRYPOINT_NAME}} auth-status # try to resolve, redacted summary
```
